Z||000000||mindscape||07-13-2001||09:59 PM||||Looking for an affordable source for a motor mount.  I'm sure mine needs to be replaced since something that looks like grease is leaking from it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||07-13-2001||10:39 PM||||Go to local auto parts store, I don't think you can find them any more affordable than $13.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mindscape||07-17-2001||10:55 PM||||I went to a local parts store.  A replacement is fairly expensive; around $68.00 for a hydraulic motor mount.  Advance tried to substitute a mount for an 1987, but the 1988 GT is different.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||07-18-2001||12:01 PM||||Make sure the grease is not oil sludge from the engine. I replaced one on my Formula with 160K miles when doing my 3.4 conversion. When I took it out it was ok. Just dirty with 13 yrs of oil leaks accumulated. Clean the area & be sure is the mount before you spend the money.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
